(An optical fiber is a cylindrical dielectric waveguide made of high-purity silica glass) Tj
T*
(\(SiO2\) that transmits optical signals via repeated Total Internal Reflection \(TIR\). In) Tj
T*
(civil engineering, optical fibers form telecommunication networks and serve as) Tj
T*
(distributed sensors embedded in concrete dams, bridge cables, and tunnels for Structural) Tj
T*
(Health Monitoring \(SHM\).) Tj
T*
(* Anatomy of an Optical Fiber: \(1\) Core: Central dielectric cylinder of high) Tj
T*
(refractive index n1. \(2\) Cladding: Surrounding coaxial dielectric sheath of slightly) Tj
T*
(lower refractive index n2 \(n1 > n2\). \(3\) Primary Buffer Jacket: Protective polymeric) Tj
T*
(acrylate coating that absorbs mechanical abrasion and moisture.) Tj
T*
(* Critical Angle \(theta_c\): By Snell's Law at core-cladding boundary: n1 *) Tj
T*
(sin\(theta_c\) = n2 * sin\(90\) => sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1.) Tj
T*
(Total internal reflection occurs only when internal ray angle of incidence phi exceeds) Tj
T*
(theta_c: phi > theta_c.) Tj
T*
