([EXAMPLE 1: Acceptance Angle and Numerical Aperture of Silica Fiber]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A step-index silica optical fiber has a core refractive index n1 =) Tj
T*
(1.480 and a cladding refractive index n2 = 1.455. The fiber launch takes place in air) Tj
T*
(\(n_0 = 1.000\). Calculate: \(1\) Critical angle theta_c at core-cladding interface, \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Numerical Aperture NA, \(3\) Acceptance angle theta_a in air, \(4\) Fractional index) Tj
T*
(difference Delta.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute Critical Angle theta_c:) Tj
T*
(sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1 = 1.455 / 1.480 = 0.98311.) Tj
T*
(theta_c = asin\(0.98311\) = 79.45 deg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Numerical Aperture NA:) Tj
T*
(NA = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) = sqrt\( \(1.480\)^2 - \(1.455\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 2.1904 - 2.117025 \) =) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(0.073375\) = 0.2709.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Acceptance Angle theta_a in air:) Tj
T*
(sin\(theta_a\) = NA = 0.2709 => theta_a = asin\(0.2709\) = 15.72 deg.) Tj
T*
(Total acceptance cone angle = 2 * theta_a = 31.44 deg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Compute Fractional Index Difference Delta:) Tj
T*
(Delta = \(n1 - n2\) / n1 = \(1.480 - 1.455\) / 1.480 = 0.025 / 1.480 = 0.01689 \(1.69%\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: theta_c = 79.45 deg; NA = 0.2709; theta_a = 15.72 deg; Delta = 1.69%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
