T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: An optical telecom link operates at laser wavelength lambda = 1.31) Tj
T*
(micrometers \(1310 nm\). The core index is n1 = 1.465 and cladding index is n2 = 1.460.) Tj
T*
(Determine: \(1\) Maximum allowable core radius a_max for single-mode operation, \(2\) If) Tj
T*
(core diameter is fabricated at 2*a = 8.0 micrometers, verify single-mode propagation and) Tj
T*
(calculate cutoff wavelength lambda_c.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute NA:) Tj
T*
(NA = sqrt\( 1.465^2 - 1.460^2 \) = sqrt\( 2.146225 - 2.1316 \) = sqrt\(0.014625\) = 0.1209.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Single-Mode Condition \(V <= 2.4048\):) Tj
T*
(V = \(2 * pi * a / lambda\) * NA <= 2.4048.) Tj
T*
(a_max = \(2.4048 * lambda\) / \(2 * pi * NA\) = \(2.4048 * 1.31 * 10^-6\) / \(2 * pi * 0.1209\)) Tj
T*
(= \(3.1503 * 10^-6\) / 0.7596 = 4.147 * 10^-6 m = 4.15 micrometers.) Tj
T*
(Maximum core diameter = 2 * a_max = 8.30 micrometers.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Verify operation for 2*a = 8.0 micrometers \(a = 4.0 micrometers\):) Tj
T*
(V = \(2 * pi * 4.0 * 10^-6 / 1.31 * 10^-6\) * 0.1209 = \(19.185\) * 0.1209 = 2.320 < 2.4048) Tj
T*
(\(Single mode confirmed!\).) Tj
T*
(Cutoff wavelength: lambda_c = \(2 * pi * a * NA\) / 2.4048 = \(2 * pi * 4.0 * 10^-6 *) Tj
T*
(0.1209\) / 2.4048 = 1.264 micrometers \(1264 nm\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Maximum core radius a_max = 4.15 micrometers; At 2*a = 8 micrometers, V =) Tj
T*
(2.320 and cutoff wavelength lambda_c = 1264 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([EXAMPLE 3: Optical Link Attenuation and Repeater Spacing]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A civil engineering fiber optic backbone connecting sensor telemetry) Tj
T*
(along a 40 km highway corridor uses single-mode fiber with attenuation coefficient alpha) Tj
T*
(= 0.22 dB/km at lambda = 1550 nm. The link has 8 fusion splices \(loss = 0.10 dB per) Tj
T*
(splice\) and two connector pairs at endpoints \(loss = 0.75 dB per connector pair\). Input) Tj
T*
(optical power is P_in = 5.0 mW \(+7 dBm\). Receiver sensitivity requires minimum P_min =) Tj
T*
(0.05 microwatts \(-43 dBm\). Determine: \(1\) Total link loss in dB, \(2\) Output power P_out,) Tj
T*
(\(3\) System safety margin.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Calculate Total Link Attenuation Loss:) Tj
T*
(Fiber cable loss = alpha * L = 0.22 dB/km * 40 km = 8.80 dB.) Tj
T*
(Splice losses = 8 * 0.10 dB = 0.80 dB.) Tj
T*
(Connector losses = 2 * 0.75 dB = 1.50 dB.) Tj
T*
(Total Link Loss alpha_total = 8.80 + 0.80 + 1.50 = 11.10 dB.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute Output Power P_out:) Tj
T*
(Total loss in dB = 10 * log10\( P_in / P_out \) => 11.10 = 10 * log10\( 5.0 mW / P_out \).) Tj
T*
(log10\( 5.0 mW / P_out \) = 1.110 => 5.0 mW / P_out = 10^\(1.110\) = 12.8825.) Tj
T*
(P_out = 5.0 mW / 12.8825 = 0.3881 mW = 388.1 microwatts.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute Power Margin above Receiver Sensitivity:) Tj
T*
(In dBm: P_out\(dBm\) = 10 * log10\(0.3881 mW / 1 mW\) = - 4.11 dBm.) Tj
T*
