(Problem Context: An industrial step-index multimode fiber has core index n1 = 1.500,) Tj
T*
(length L = 3.0 km, and fractional index contrast Delta = 0.010 \(1.0%\). Calculate: \(1\)) Tj
T*
(Minimum and maximum transit times of light rays through the fiber, \(2\) Total intermodal) Tj
T*
(pulse broadening Delta t_modal, \(3\) Maximum theoretical bit rate B_max without) Tj
T*
(inter-symbol interference.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Transit Times for Axial and Highest-Order Rays:) Tj
T*
(Speed of light in core: v = c / n1 = \(3.0 * 10^8 m/s\) / 1.500 = 2.0 * 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Minimum transit time \(axial direct ray\): t_min = L / v = \(L * n1\) / c = \(3000 m * 1.50\)) Tj
T*
(/ \(3.0 * 10^8 m/s\) = 1.50 * 10^-5 s = 15.0 microseconds.) Tj
T*
(Maximum transit time \(steepest zigzag ray at critical angle theta_c\): t_max = \(L * n1^2\)) Tj
T*
(/ \(c * n2\) ~= t_min / \(1 - Delta\).) Tj
T*
(t_max = 1.50 * 10^-5 / \(1 - 0.010\) = 1.50 * 10^-5 / 0.99 = 1.51515 * 10^-5 s = 15.1515) Tj
T*
(microseconds.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Pulse Broadening Delta t_modal:) Tj
T*
(Delta t_modal = t_max - t_min = \(L * n1 / c\) * Delta = \(1.50 * 10^-5 s\) * 0.010 = 1.50 *) Tj
T*
(10^-7 s = 150 nanoseconds.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Maximum Bit Rate B_max:) Tj
T*
(To prevent pulses from overlapping, bit duration T_bit >= 2 * Delta t_modal:) Tj
T*
(B_max ~= 1 / \(2 * Delta t_modal\) = 1 / \(2 * 150 * 10^-9 s\) = 1 / \(3.0 * 10^-7 s\) = 3.33) Tj
T*
(* 10^6 bits/s = 3.33 Mbps.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Intermodal delay spread Delta t = 150 ns; Maximum data rate is limited to) Tj
T*
(3.33 Mbps over 3 km.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.8 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Derive expressions for Numerical Aperture and Acceptance Angle of a step-index) Tj
T*
(optical fiber.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Consider a cylindrical fiber with core index n1 and cladding n2 \(n1 > n2\) in an) Tj
T*
(ambient medium of index n0. A ray enters the core face at angle theta_0 and refracts at) Tj
T*
(angle r. At the core-cladding interface, the angle of incidence is phi = 90 - r. For) Tj
T*
(total internal reflection to occur, phi >= theta_c, where sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1. At the) Tj
T*
(critical limit phi = theta_c, cos\(r\) = sin\(phi\) = n2 / n1. By Snell's law at entrance:) Tj
T*
(n0 * sin\(theta_a\) = n1 * sin\(r\) = n1 * sqrt\(1 - cos^2\(r\)\) = n1 * sqrt\(1 - \(n2/n1\)^2\) =) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\). For air launch \(n0 = 1.0\): sin\(theta_a\) = sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\).) Tj
T*
(Numerical Aperture is defined as NA = sin\(theta_a\) = sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\). The acceptance) Tj
T*
(angle is theta_a = asin\(sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\)\).) Tj
T*
