(* Q2: Explain the working principle of Fiber Bragg Grating \(FBG\) sensors and their) Tj
T*
(direct engineering utility in Civil Structural Health Monitoring.) Tj
T*
(Answer: An FBG sensor is created by exposing the germanium-doped silica core of a) Tj
T*
(single-mode fiber to a periodic ultraviolet laser interference pattern, inducing a) Tj
T*
(permanent periodic modulation of refractive index of spatial pitch Lambda. When) Tj
T*
(broadband light travels down the fiber, a narrow spectral peak is reflected at the Bragg) Tj
T*
(wavelength: lambda_B = 2 * n_eff * Lambda. When the host civil structure undergoes) Tj
T*
(mechanical strain or temperature fluctuations, the physical pitch Lambda stretches or) Tj
T*
